  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts an elderly woman falling on the floor, with text overlay that reads 'when you floor it but your passengers aren't ready.' The visual of an older woman falling is juxtaposed with the phrase 'floor it,' which is a driving term implying sudden acceleration. The meme uses this contrast to imply that the woman is clumsy or unprepared, which can be interpreted as mocking her physical abilities. This portrayal of an older woman as uncoordinated or incapable of handling sudden movements is a form of age-based stereotyping and can be considered misogynous, as it reinforces negative stereotypes about older women's physical competence and stability. The meme's intent is to create humor by highlighting the perceived clumsiness of older women, which can be seen as demeaning and potentially harmful to older women, contributing to ageist and misogynous attitudes.",
